      "body": "## Summary\n\nMake `test_draft_layer_rows_mirrored_after_drafter` independent of the active hardware platform by injecting a mock HiSparse backend before constructing `HiSparseConnectorWorker`.\n\nPR #62592 moved backend selection into the worker constructor. The test currently installs only a method mock after construction, so Intel BMG nightly CI now fails first with `RuntimeError: The current platform does not support HiSparse` even though the test uses CPU tensors and a fake DMA implementation.\n\n## Failure evidence\n\nNightly main build #97886, Intel BMG V1 shard 2:\n\n- `test_draft_layer_rows_mirrored_after_drafter[FULL]`\n- `test_draft_layer_rows_mirrored_after_drafter[NONE]`\n\nBoth fail during `HiSparseConnectorWorker(...)`, before reaching the test's existing fake `swap_blocks_batch` implementation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- full file-scoped pre-commit suite for `tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_connector.py`\n- exact Intel BMG V1 validation required before merge\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
